Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-10-2001||12:09 PM||||A few of my fuses are really loose in the fusebox.. anyway to tighten them up or would I need to replace my fuse box?<P><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-10-2001||12:38 PM||||First, disconnect the battery.  That way when you are working on the fusebox you won't accidentally short something out.  Next, the only way that a fuse will be loose is when the little connectors inside the box don't have much 'spring' left in them, that is that they don't clamp down tight enough on the fuse.  I would suggest using a pair of needle nose pliers to try and bend the holders back closed.<P>I've never heard of any fusebox doing this, do you have any idea's why yours is like that?||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-10-2001||01:10 PM||||Thanks for the info.. I will try that..<P>No idea why it started, It never did it before I had it stored..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-10-2001||07:40 PM||||They are loose pluging/unplugging or they just wiggle? The terminals are loose in the plastic fuse block. They will often wiggle some. As long as they plug in tight then don't worry about it. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-10-2001||08:29 PM||||nope really loose...  ex: my dome light fuse fell out the other day..  I pushed it in tight but its still jiggly and loses contact even when its in....   I never had this happen before to any vehicle..<P>||||reg||1
